WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:10.620
Climate change is often talked about, yet the change in the seasons—warmer winters and hotter summers—may not be noticed because it happens very slowly.
人们常常谈论气候变化，然而季节的变化——冬天更暖、夏天更热——却可能不会引起注意，因为这种变化发生得非常缓慢。

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.180
Studies show people don’t notice slow changes easily.
研究表明，人们不容易注意到缓慢的变化。

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.290
The story of Princeton is a good example.
普林斯顿的故事就是一个很好的例子。

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.060
In the past, Lake Carnegie froze every winter.
过去，卡内基湖每年冬天都会结冰。

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.930
People in Princeton could skate on the thick ice through winter.
普林斯顿的人们整个冬天都可以在厚厚的冰面上滑冰。

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:30.830
However, around the 1970s, winters in Princeton started to become warmer.
然而，大约在20世纪70年代，普林斯顿的冬天开始变暖了。

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.860
Now, the lake seldom freezes, so people cannot skate on it every winter.
如今，这个湖很少结冰，所以人们无法每年冬天都在湖上滑冰。

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.610
But most people there didn’t connect this with climate change.
但那里的大多数人并没有把这件事和气候变化联系起来。

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:47.560
The real-life example helped researchers look for a better way to get people to notice slow changes brought by climate change.
这个现实生活中的例子帮助研究人员寻找更好的方法，让人们注意到气候变化带来的缓慢变化。

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.470
In their research, they showed volunteers two different graphs—a temperature graph and a lake-freezing graph.
在研究中，他们给志愿者看了两张不同的图表——一张气温图和一张湖泊结冰图。

00:00:55.270 --> 00:01:00.000
The temperature graph showed a fictional town’s rising winter temperatures over the years.
气温图显示的是一个虚构小镇多年来不断上升的冬季气温。

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.300
The lake-freezing graph showed whether the town’s lake froze each year.
湖泊结冰图显示的是这个小镇的湖每年是否结冰。

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.550
Both graphs showed the same climate trend, but they made the volunteers feel differently.
两张图表显示的是相同的气候趋势，却让志愿者产生了不同的感受。

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:19.420
When the volunteers saw the lake-freezing graph, they felt climate change was more serious, because they could directly see the lake didn’t freeze every year like before.
志愿者看到湖泊结冰图时，觉得气候变化更严重，因为他们能直接看到，湖没有像以前那样每年都结冰。

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.180
This helped them see the influence of climate change clearly.
这帮助他们清楚地看到了气候变化的影响。

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:32.360
But when the volunteers saw the temperature graph, they didn’t feel the same, because the graph failed to help them connect climate change with daily life.
但志愿者看到气温图时，却没有同样的感受，因为这张图没能帮助他们把气候变化和日常生活联系起来。

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:39.950
With the help of what the research has found, we can actively notice slow changes in our daily life brought by climate change.
借助这项研究的发现，我们可以主动留意日常生活中气候变化带来的缓慢变化。

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:44.560
At the same time, we can also help the people around us notice them.
同时，我们也可以帮助身边的人注意到这些变化。
